MathCAT (intent, en): lim inf / lim sup read as "the limit inferior/superior as"

1. The `limit` intent rule names lim sup / lim inf `limit-sup` /
   `limit-inf`, but every language's definitions.yaml defines them as
   `lim-sup` / `lim-inf` (en: "the limit inferior as"). No definition
   matched, so the bare name was spoken: "limit inf n right arrow
   infinity". The rule now produces the names the languages define.
2. en unicode.yaml reads "→" as "approaches" only under a `limit`; under
   `lim-inf`/`lim-sup` too now ("as n approaches infinity").

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37. Worth
proposing upstream to daisy/MathCAT.

diff --git a/Rules/Intent/general.yaml b/Rules/Intent/general.yaml
index e1652158..6706a3c3 100644
--- a/Rules/Intent/general.yaml
+++ b/Rules/Intent/general.yaml
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@
   match: "*[1][$NoSpacesBase='lim' or $NoSpacesBase='limsup' or $NoSpacesBase='liminf']"
   replace: 
   - intent:
-      xpath-name: "IfThenElse($NoSpacesBase='lim', 'limit', IfThenElse($NoSpacesBase='limsup', 'limit-sup', 'limit-inf'))"
+      xpath-name: "IfThenElse($NoSpacesBase='lim', 'limit', IfThenElse($NoSpacesBase='limsup', 'lim-sup', 'lim-inf'))"
       attrs: "data-intent-property='concat(data-intent-property, \":prefix:\")'"
       children: [x: "*[2]"]
 
diff --git a/Rules/Languages/en/unicode.yaml b/Rules/Languages/en/unicode.yaml
index f9b39fb2..055b0ce8 100644
--- a/Rules/Languages/en/unicode.yaml
+++ b/Rules/Languages/en/unicode.yaml
@@ -333,7 +333,7 @@
  - "↑": [t: "up arrow"]                       # 0x2191
  - "→":                                          # 0x2192
      - test:
-        if: "ancestor::*[2][self::m:limit]"
+        if: "ancestor::*[2][self::m:limit or self::m:lim-inf or self::m:lim-sup]"
         then: [t: "approaches"]
         else: [t: "right arrow"]
 
